      "parameters": {
        "content": "## NWI - Deal -> BC Customer + Sales Order: set up before publishing\n1. Webhook node: connect header-auth credential **NWI HubSpot Webhook Auth** (see the HubSpot header note in the PR). Publish, then point the HubSpot webhook subscription (Deal property `dealstage`) at the PRODUCTION URL.\n2. Connect credentials: **NWI HubSpot App Token** (HubSpot app token, scopes: crm.objects.deals.read/write, companies.read/write, contacts.read, line_items read) and **Business Central – NWI Group (client credentials)** on every HTTP node. Confirm no \"not connected\" warning remains on any node.\n3. *Workflow Config* holds the BC tenant ID, environment (Production) and company GUID. Check they are right. Its `triggers` list (dealstage=closedwon, hs_is_closed_won=true, closed_won=true) says which property changes start the sync: subscribe the HubSpot webhook to one of them.\n4. Settings -> Error Workflow: set the shared error handler.\n5. Confirm HubSpot properties exist: company `business_central_id`, deal `bc_order_id` (single-line text). \n6. Confirm BC item numbers equal HubSpot line item SKUs.\n\n**Real time, no fan-out:** one deal per execution. Order lines go to BC in one call.\n**Re-run safe:** deal with bc_order_id set is skipped; BC order is looked up by deal ID before creating.",
